# 85. ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWERS

### Active Directory

> Active Directory is Microsoft's directory service that centrally manages identities, computers, groups, authentication, authorization and policies in Windows domain environments.

### Kerberoasting

> Kerberoasting is a technique that targets Kerberos service accounts associated with SPNs and can allow offline password guessing against obtained service-ticket material.

### AS-REP Roasting

> AS-REP roasting targets accounts configured without Kerberos preauthentication and can expose material suitable for offline password guessing.

### Pass-the-Hash

> Pass-the-Hash is an authentication attack in which a stolen NTLM hash is reused without requiring recovery of the plaintext password.

### Pass-the-Ticket

> Pass-the-Ticket involves unauthorized reuse of stolen Kerberos authentication tickets.

### BloodHound

> BloodHound is a graph-based tool used to visualize Active Directory relationships and identify potential attack paths.

### Lateral Movement

> Lateral movement is the process of moving from one compromised system or identity to another within an environment.

